title: A stranger who starts at 'docs/README.org' with no AI stops first at its opening, and for good at setup's first step, which names a file that is not there.
pid: b249fb9b-ac00-4c87-802f-a3de697c41b6
body: |2-
  Read on 2026-11-15 at commit f50eb4e0, as someone who has heard skg
  is worth trying, knows Emacs or Neovim and Org, and has no AI and
  nobody to ask, going from installing it to a first note, a first
  link, and a first view of someone else's notes. I installed nothing,
  and read no code, nor the scripts the pages send the reader to.
  The stops are below in the order the reader meets them, each with
  what would carry the reader past it. The measure was Tay's
  [[id:ea18ac3f-6f8a-43bb-a6bc-3279c417e9ca][How he explains to a stranger: eight habits]]; a letter in brackets, as (c), names one of them.
  The first hard stop is the fourth: until the Docker step is fixed,
  nothing after it is reached by anyone reading alone.
